{"ts":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"93c1cb9c51cd52f327b34f44","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-1jzupz"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Assurance primitives: measurements, invariants, and gates become declarative pm data evaluated by the SDK, so a project's quality contract is configuration instead of bespoke scripts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Every quality property this project enforces is expressed as a hand-written .mjs script that shells out to pm. 16 files match *gate*.mjs and carry 6,500 LOC; 55 scripts total carry 16,184 LOC; 20 of them drive the pm CLI as a subprocess to recompute properties over .agents/pm that the SDK already holds in memory. The gate inventory itself is derived by regex over human-written GitHub workflow step names, so a gate's identity is its title in prose and renaming a step silently changes the inventory. None of this is available to any other project: a team adopting pm inherits the item model and inherits none of the assurance model, and an agent cannot add, retune, or scope a bound without writing Node. Declaring a measurable property over the record, comparing it to a filed number, and recording the verdict IS project management under this project's own philosophy, so it belongs in the SDK as a primitive with a CLI surface and a data-declared registry. The primitive set is measure (name a population), assert (bound it), gate (bundle bounds behind a lifecycle trigger), and a verdict record appended to the immutable history. Every part is data an agent can author with pm commands and jq, extended by provider plugins so a coverage percentage, a benchmark millisecond, an eval score, an RL episode reward, or a registry dist-tag are all measurable and enforceable on the same terms as an item count."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:governance","area:sdk","assurance","configurability","enforcement","measurement-ratchet","universal"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":2400},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The full assurance model is declarable as workspace data through pm commands, with no repository code required to add, retune, scope, or retire a bound; The SDK exposes the primitives so the CLI, MCP, and any embedding host evaluate identical semantics, and the CLI adds no assurance logic of its own; This repository dogfoods the result: every bespoke gate script is either retired onto the primitives or carries a recorded disposition explaining why it cannot be; A gate's identity is a declared id in the registry, never a workflow step title, and the inventory is derived from the registry rather than from prose pattern-matching; Presets make the model usable on a new project in one command for at least software-delivery, research, agent-environment, and operations shapes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":80},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-33cw","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-4vz6mz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-8jdc","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-9gzr4r","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-klxax7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-kpftft","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-mj42og","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-o0sqz5","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-t4d7nz","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-usfg","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:05.456Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3def9990aab690dce1f59a9d82867efc31eb6b69501dc25ab7c2a038a6f99e81","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T20:58:39.520Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"93c1cb9c51cd52f327b34f44","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T20:58:39.520Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-10T20:58:39.520Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Measured surface at filing time (2026-08-10): 55 .mjs files under scripts/ totalling 16,184 lines; 16 files match *gate*.mjs totalling 6,500 lines; 20 scripts invoke the pm CLI as a subprocess to recompute properties over .agents/pm. scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs alone is 929 lines and holds 30 declarations across 5 hard-coded selector sources (dependency_kind, validate_warning, graph_profile, graph_finding, health_check) — none of which can address any population the graph ANALYTICS compute, so redundancy_count, articulation_count, bridge_count and community_count are computable and unbounded. A prototype adding a sixth source was written and reverted during this session precisely because the capability belongs in the SDK, not in a script: the same 80 lines of selector plumbing would have to be rewritten by every project that adopts pm."}]}],"before_hash":"3def9990aab690dce1f59a9d82867efc31eb6b69501dc25ab7c2a038a6f99e81","after_hash":"72d68480d57293d309b4f38da83c45031e5e4796ee6329c63aa06276ceb564e9"}
