{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-12T20:13:26.234Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ef0a31908b232616bff09378","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.269","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-09-12T20:13:26.234Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Measurement design input 2026-09-12: the pm-user skill mandates a create-time duplicate-check comment that names the nearest existing owners, and the prose-edge-gaps measurement counts every id in that comment as a gap, so six correctly filed items raised the observed count by 24 against a ceiling with zero headroom. The exemption list is the only relief and it is per holder, so each new item needs an exemption row that says the same thing. A declared convention (a comment prefix or a comment kind such as duplicate_check) that the prose scanner treats as inventory rather than assertion would remove the per-item ceremony; until then, new items are exempted and the ceiling is tightened to the observed value after each pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-12T20:13:26.234Z"}],"before_hash":"0d2bef929cc1ebf3efe2501a71e9a723fff37cc61dce424805ed6914777437ae","after_hash":"385eb25a81e12770b35a09a1897353d5aa85600783b8cdc6c432cffa85dd84f4","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ab7435d53b516b80b61fb6cd4150727a458581e03015578f84021e1160aca8bd"}
